> 
> 
> The specific names (#name-y) are (at least in some cases) considered to be
> actually written on the items, while the generic names supposedly are
> something the character keeps in their head. Fruitnames, being configured via
> options, are probably supposed to actually define the type of fruit found
> (though nutrition and weight are, of course, fixed), so that the adventurer
> having pineapples as their fruits and finding a bones pile of someone having
> kiwis will actually posses pineapples and kiwis (which by some miracle have
> exactly identical properties).

More over all fruits that have existed in the game are wishable. So if 
that character eats the kiwis he found in the bones file and wants to 
have more of them he can wish them.

